 matches the spec, so I merged branch `local-agent/j-20261016-fde7e1` with `git merge --ff-only`.\n\n- **`datasette/default_actions.py`:** I added the `create-view` and `drop-view` actions.\n- **`datasette/write_sql.py`:** `create view` now requires `create-view` on the database. `drop view` requires `drop-view` on the view as a table resource.\n- **`datasette/utils/sql_analysis.py`:** the suppressed-delete set is now `dropped_tables_and_views`. The spurious delete SQLite reports when a view is dropped no longer becomes a `delete-row` requirement.\n- **`docs/authentication.rst`:** the `--root` permission list and the two new action sections are added.\n\nI ran only the spec's test file, not the rest of the suite. In the docs, the `drop-view` heading underline is one character longer than the title, which RST accepts.", "ttft_ms": 3078, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 126032, "uuid": "c7692efb-0c6a-4b03-ac51-9e2ff5972836", "ttft_stream_ms": 2347, "time_to_request_ms": 50, "first_content_frame_ms": 2347, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
